shortAnswer: "Guardrails are the limits placed around an AI system: what it can reach, what it can act on, what it must refuse, and what needs a human before it happens. The ones that matter in a business aren't inside the model — they're the boundaries you set around it, and they're mostly about access and approval rather than clever instructions."
faq:
